Subject: [PATCH 08/31] feat: ISO passthrough, centre autofocus, yaw-aligned
 anchoring

- Lens packet's reserved field now carries ISO (0 = older app, ignored);
  forwarded to the cinematic camera and shown in the debug overlay.
- Centre autofocus: one-shot eLensFlag_AutofocusRequest raycasts the
  scene along the camera axis (500 m, miss racks to infinity), sets the
  focus distance and reports it back with eControlCmd_SetFocus so the
  phone fader follows. The renderer's own ~0.3 s DOF easing provides the
  focus rack glide.
- Align Yaw On Start (default on): anchoring cancels only the heading of
  the captured phone/entity poses, keeping pitch/roll gravity-aligned so
  turning the phone always rotates the entity about world up.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017nykaDjTHxHDSo11CsYx6M
